# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 10 ("A `Prelude.Unwrap` answers each `~ x` with `x`", whatever answers the family) and ch. 9 (a request at tick n is answered as an input of tick n+1, which is owed), in the Test World's spelling of a delivery. Never run when written.
test an_unwrap_is_answered_a_tick_later

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="tap")
    1: Prelude.Unwrap
    2: Ui.Label(text="heard 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  requested:
    1: ~ 1

tick 2
  in:
    1: 1
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="heard 1")

tick 3
  in:
    0: click
  requested:
    1: ~ 2

compute until idle: 1 tick, 4 to 4

tick 4
  in:
    1: 2
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="heard 2")
